    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`_verify_combine_stage2` merges the prefix splits with weights `exp(lse - max)`. A split whose KV range is empty skips the stage1 store of `Att_Out` and only writes the `-inf` lse sentinel, so its weight is 0. Stage2 still loads that split's `Att_Out` row, which holds whatever the reused scratch buffer (`VerifySplitKV.att_out`, cached per shape in `_VK_CACHE`) last contained, and computes `ao * 0`. If that stale memory is nan or inf, `0 * nan = nan` and the whole draft row of the output becomes nan.\n\nEmpty splits are routine, not a corner case. A split covers whole 32-key blocks, so:\n\n- with 4 splits, any prefix of 96 keys or fewer leaves at least one split empty;\n- with 16 splits (chosen from the batch-average prefix, so a long request in the batch selects it), a short request in the same batch leaves most of its splits empty. For example, a 100-key prefix fills 4 of 16.\n\nThe cached buffer is allocated with `torch.empty`, so its first contents come from the caching allocator and are not guaranteed finite. Raising the split cap, as proposed in #35521, makes empty splits more frequent.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `verify_splitkv.py`: in stage2, load `Att_Out` only where the split is valid (`lse > -inf`), with `other=0.0`. Valid splits are unchanged, so results on inputs that were already finite are bit-identical.\n- `test_verify_splitkv.py`: add `test_empty_splits_ignore_stale_scratch`. It fills the cached `att_out` with nan, then runs the existing parity check against `extend_attention_fwd` for prefixes `[64]` (4 splits, 2 empty) and `[16384, 100]` (16 splits, 12 empty for the short request).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nI ran the registered test file on MI325X (gfx942) with upstream `main` at eae134d61f, in `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-rocm720-mi30x`. The kernel and test files are identical between that tag and `main`; `main`'s `python/` was used via `PYTHONPATH`.\n\n| tree | result |\n|---|---|\n| `main` + new test only | 2 failed (both `test_empty_splits_ignore_stale_scratch` subtests), 10 passed |\n| `main` + fix + new test | 10 passed, 14 subtests passed (3 consecutive runs) |\n\nThe fix only adds a load mask, so I did not run separate end-to-end accuracy tests. Every existing parity case passes unchanged.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThis adds one compare and one extra mask term to a load that was already masked, in the small combine kernel. I did not measure a change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No user-facing change.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39422688754](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39422688754)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39422688952](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39422688952)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39422688902](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39422688902)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->