      "body": "Cross-check with #35521 (split-KV verify on gfx942, with a CU-aware split cap of up to 128), on MI325X with the SGLang v0.5.22 gfx942 image (`lmsysorg/sglang@sha256:aa8e2ceb88a5ec7ed2d54dce8eca1b17b11ec57c686a37217df9bf938dbab01c`, ROCm 7.2.4).\n\nThe shape is Qwen3.8-27B TP1 target-verify: 24 / 4 heads, head_dim 256, 4 draft tokens, fp8 paged KV. We filled every cached `att_out` scratch buffer with nan, then reran short-prefix calls: `[64]`, `[100]`, `[16384, 100]` and `[131072, 77]`.\n\n| tree | cases with a nan output |\n|---|---:|\n| `main` (6cac4dc3fe) | 3 / 4 |\n| `main` + #35521 | 4 / 4 |\n| `main` + #35521 + this PR | 0 / 4 (all equal to the clean run) |\n\n#35521 raises the split count for small batches, so more splits end up empty, and `[100]` now fails as well. On 9 latency/accuracy cases (bs 1-48, prefixes from 8k to 128k, and a mixed batch), this PR on top of #35521 gives identical error statistics against an fp32 reference. Per-call latency is within 1%, except 1 x 8k at +6% (0.003 ms). The two PRs merge cleanly except for the test file: the imports and adjacent new tests.\n",
